    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Phantom Frequencies - Signalis",
    "description": "Return to the abandoned radio station, rebuilt from the ground up.\r\n\r\nThis remake expands the original scene with fully reworked lighting, depth, and detail, transforming it from a static moment into a living, atmospheric space. Cold winds sweep across the mountains outside while the station hums quietly, caught between silence and signal.\r\n\r\n[hr][/hr]\r\n\r\n[h2]Features[/h2]\r\n\r\n• Fully remade 3D scene with improved lighting and depth  \r\n• Dynamic environment effects: snow, wind, and glass grime  \r\n• Post-processing controls including film grain and optional bloom  \r\n• Audio visualizer with customisable bars, spacing, and colour  \r\n• Ambient sound effects and adjustable volume controls  \r\n• Optional music tracks:\r\n  - Home  \r\n  - Die Toteninsel  \r\n  - Double Back (VHS)  \r\n\r\n[hr][/hr]\r\n\r\n[h2]Desk Customisation[/h2]\r\n\r\n• 3 Polaroid options + custom image support  \r\n• 5 book variations  \r\n• 2 in-game manuals  \r\n• Toggleable desk elements and props  \r\n• Customisable lamp colour and intensity  \r\n• Subtle flicker and environmental interaction  \r\n\r\n[hr][/hr]\r\n\r\n[h2]Atmosphere[/h2]\r\n\r\nThe lamp casts a soft, adjustable glow across the desk, grounding the scene in a quiet, uneasy warmth. The world outside remains cold and distant, visible through the station window.\r\n\r\nOccasionally, the signal breaks, revealing 1 of 22 fragmented, corrupted transmissions from elsewhere.\r\n\r\n[hr][/hr]\r\n\r\nThis is not just a remaster.  \r\nIt is a reconstruction of memory, signal, and silence.",
